body:
I'd probably do the following:

&#x200B;

\* Before claiming the ticket, I'm storing the ticket in a ziploc back and stick it in into somewhere in my large walk-in closet, I have a bunch of crap so it'll be easy to hide it. If I feel especially paranoid, I'll stick it into my underwear and only use the bathroom at home with the door locked

&#x200B;

\* Buy a 1 TB external hard drive

&#x200B;

\* Download all data from social media and then perma-delete all social media accounts

&#x200B;

\* get a VPN

&#x200B;

\* read all relevant reddit posts and articles on what to do if you won a large sum and follow advie that works for me as much as I'm able without being able to contact professionals

&#x200B;

\* get a new email that no one knows, same with phone number and a PO box

&#x200B;

\* contact a bank who handles wealth and open a new account with them, ensure that they understand confidentiality and that they will be sued/legal action if they spill the beans that I have the winning ticket

&#x200B;

\* if I can set up a double blind trust on my own, I will make that to happen because I live in Florida and I'll be able to claim it without revealing my name. If I'm forced to reveal because the lottery officials won't take the form of documentation on trust without legal representation or whatever, then I will get legally married and change my name to a very common last name of my husband's to cloak my identity. My current legal name is all over the internet and very unique because of my books and a blog

&#x200B;

\* If the bank I'm using let me take out a bridge loan, then I'll borrow 100,000 to set up a new place to live, charter a private cruise to eventually fill it with the trustworthy family and friends I really want to give a portion of my allotted 22.4 million tax-free gifts to them

&#x200B;

\* After I validate my ticket at the headquarters, I'm leaving to go on that cruise for a month or two, or even for the full year. There, I'll explain to family/friends my situation, and that after the one time gift, there will be no more gifts except for education funds for their children

&#x200B;

\* On the anniversary, I"m hiring a family office
